data: {"type":"node-end","node_id":"budget_expert","output":{"result":"**Clothing/Apparel List**\n\n*   **Underwear**: 3 pairs ($30-$60)\n*   **Socks**: 3 pairs (wool or synthetic, ski-specific) ($45-$75)\n*   **Base Layers (tops and bottoms)**: 2 sets (mid-weight, wool or synthetic) ($150-$300)\n*   **Mid-Layers**: 1-2 (fleece jacket, insulated vest, or synthetic pullover) ($80-$250)\n*   **Ski Jacket**: (waterproof, insulated) ($200-$800)\n*   **Ski Pants**: (waterproof, insulated) ($150-$600)\n*   **Warm Hat or Beanie**: (wool or fleece) ($20-$50)\n*   **Gloves or Mittens**: (waterproof, insulated) ($60-$200)\n*   **Neck Gaiter or Balaclava**: (fleece or wool) ($20-$50)\n*   **Goggles**: (UV protection, anti-fog) ($60-$200)\n*   **Casual wear for evenings**: (jeans, sweater, comfortable shoes) ($100-$300)\n\n**Ski Gear List**\n\n*   **Skis**: (all-mountain, appropriate length) ($400-$1000 to buy, $120-$200 for 3-day rental)\n*   **Ski Boots**: (comfortable, appropriate fit) ($300-$800 to buy, $90-$150 for 3-day rental)\n*   **Ski Bindings**: (DIN setting appropriate for weight/skill) (usually included with skis)\n*   **Ski Poles**: (appropriate length) ($40-$100 to buy, $15-$30 for 3-day rental)\n*   **Helmet**: (ski-specific, MIPS recommended) ($80-$250 to buy, $30-$50 for 3-day rental)\n*   **Ski Lock**: (small, retractable) ($15-$30)\n*   **Backpack**: (small daypack for water, snacks, extra layer) ($30-$100)\n\n**Accessories/Miscellaneous**\n\n*   **Sunscreen**: (high SPF, for face and lips) ($10-$20)\n*   **Lip Balm**: (with SPF) ($5-$10)\n*   **Portable Charger**: (for phone/gopro) ($30-$80)\n*   **Hand Warmers**: (optional) ($10-$20)","extra_info":{"usage":{"prompt_tokens":67,"completion_tokens":592,"total_tokens":659},"tool_calls":null,"all_tasks":[{"id":"8f9e1976-9b4c-49b9-a1dd-bf5a6de48868","task_name":"Compile a comprehensive list of clothing and apparel suitable for a 3-day ski trip in Aspen, Colorado, considering cold weather and snow conditions.","a